descriptionByLocale.en:
The resource will work within the Pharmaceutical Technology function, following the formulative development activities of pharmaceutical products, chemical-physical characterization and stability studies to industrial scale-up and batch preparation for clinical trials.

Mansions:

- It will develop new pharmaceutical formulations and review product formulations already on the market;

- It will perform chemical-physical studies and characterizations of products in the development phase;

- It will monitor the stability of products and raw materials during the phases of development of the pharmaceutical form;

- It will collaborate with raw material suppliers, providing technical support during formulative development activities;

- It will follow the industrial scale-up activities of pharmaceutical products, from laboratory to production;

- It will provide technical documentation and set up lots for clinical trials.

Profile required:

- Degree in Chemistry and Pharmaceutical Technology (CTF);

- Experimental thesis in Pharmaceutical Technique or work experience in the field of formulative development;

- Experience in formulative aspects and pharmaceutical development processes;

- Basic knowledge of GMP regulations and ICH guidelines;

- Basic knowledge of production plants;

- Good knowledge of the main IT tools (Excel, Word and PowerPoint);

- Good knowledge of English.

Personal skills and skills:

- Accuracy and attention to details;

- Analytical approach and guidance on troubleshooting;

- Ability to work in teams and collaborate with internal and external partners;

- Proactivity and orientation to the result.

descriptionByLocale.de:
